    <meta name="description" id="metaDesc" content="Founded by Alexander the Great in 331 BC, Alexandria, Egypt, has been a cultural and intellectual hub for centuries. Situated on the Mediterranean coast, this coastal city, often called the “Bride of the Mediterranean,” is renowned for its rich history, diverse culture, and significant role in the ancient world. Today, it remains a vibrant and cosmopolitan city." />
